# SYNTAX TEST "source.tiddlywiki5.tid-file" "A broken value cannot swallow the field beneath it"
# Opening every header value to wikitext raises one hazard above miscolour: a body rule reaching
# past the end of a field. Pandoc met it — a Markdown title ending in two spaces took the hard-
# linebreak rule, ate the field boundary, and put the date into the author field.
#
# It cannot reach here. A value reads inside a capture, and a capture confines to its own span, so
# a construct left open at the end of a line closes with the line. Each pair below leaves one open
# and asks the field under it to read as a field.
